WEBVTT

00:00:01.520 --> 00:00:04.310
Satoshi and Go
came to the Galar Region...

00:00:04.730 --> 00:00:08.190
...to watch the Supreme Monarch
Dande’s battle.

00:00:08.190 --> 00:00:12.270
After the match, the two encountered
and battled a Galarian Kamonegi,

00:00:12.270 --> 00:00:14.490
and Satoshi ended up catching it.

00:00:15.870 --> 00:00:20.200
What new encounters await them today,
on the second day of their trip?

00:00:21.540 --> 00:00:24.250
It’s Galar’s famous Curry Rice!

00:00:24.250 --> 00:00:26.760
Boiled Egg Curry and
Kyodaimax Curry!

00:00:26.760 --> 00:00:30.000
There’s Plenty-of-Potatoes Curry
and Tropical Curry, too!

00:00:32.510 --> 00:00:32.910
Shoot City, Galar Region

00:00:32.910 --> 00:00:35.230
Let’s dig in!
Shoot City, Galar Region

00:00:35.230 --> 00:00:36.680
Shoot City, Galar Region

00:00:37.870 --> 00:00:39.680
It’s totally amazing!

00:00:40.070 --> 00:00:42.980
It’s like it’s melting on
my tongue!

00:01:04.040 --> 00:01:05.560
Huh? What’s up?

00:01:05.560 --> 00:01:07.340
Picking up from yesterday?

00:01:14.970 --> 00:01:18.730
Hey, you can battle <i>after</i> we’ve eaten!

00:01:31.920 --> 00:01:33.160
What’s this?

00:01:33.160 --> 00:01:35.100
I’ve never seen
this Pokémon before!

00:01:38.750 --> 00:01:39.950
It’s crying!

00:01:39.950 --> 00:01:41.790
Maybe it’s still a kid?

00:01:42.360 --> 00:01:45.020
I wonder what this Pokémon
is called...!

00:01:45.020 --> 00:01:45.790
Satoshi...

00:01:46.170 --> 00:01:48.180
Why are you crying?

00:01:48.180 --> 00:01:51.770
I dunno...
My tears just won’t stop...

00:01:51.770 --> 00:01:52.870
But you’re crying, too...

00:01:52.870 --> 00:01:55.380
Huh? Me too? Why?!

00:02:07.520 --> 00:02:08.600
It vanished!

00:02:10.560 --> 00:02:12.060
Did it run away...?

00:02:12.060 --> 00:02:13.300
Let’s find it!

00:02:13.300 --> 00:02:14.440
Yeah!

00:02:14.570 --> 00:02:21.200
PocketMonsters

00:02:21.200 --> 00:02:23.620
Hey, you still not ready? C'mon, hurry up!

00:02:23.620 --> 00:02:26.200
You all packed and ready to leave?

00:02:26.200 --> 00:02:28.920
I'll show you this wide mysterious world

00:02:28.920 --> 00:02:31.790
And skip the slow send-off

00:02:31.790 --> 00:02:34.130
Be it through fire or through water

00:02:34.130 --> 00:02:36.800
I'm fumbling blindly through the days

00:02:36.800 --> 00:02:41.300
When I don't even know what the next second will bring

00:02:41.970 --> 00:02:46.560
Each and every one of my memories

00:02:46.560 --> 00:02:51.150
Can always be found inside a Ball

00:02:52.310 --> 00:02:55.070
On 1, 2, 3, dive in!

00:02:55.070 --> 00:03:00.820
I've got the future plans I imagined in my pocket

00:03:02.780 --> 00:03:07.830
Greeting someone new is always fresh

00:03:07.830 --> 00:03:12.040
No need (No need!) to hesitate! Try! (Try!)

00:03:12.040 --> 00:03:13.380
Let's have a fight!

00:03:13.380 --> 00:03:16.090
1: Once the battle's done

00:03:16.090 --> 00:03:17.920
2: And we're laughing or crying

00:03:17.920 --> 00:03:22.260
On 3, let's be friends!

00:03:23.550 --> 00:03:28.930
Any day and every day, that's always been my rule

00:03:28.930 --> 00:03:34.270
With this unpredictable, boundless world awaiting

00:03:34.270 --> 00:03:36.770
Let's go! Every time you trip and fall

00:03:36.770 --> 00:03:40.900
Let's go! You pick yourself up by my side

00:03:40.900 --> 00:03:42.700
I choose you!

00:03:46.280 --> 00:03:51.710
Sobbing Messon

00:03:53.120 --> 00:03:54.790
Where could it have gone?

00:03:54.790 --> 00:03:55.960
Hey, Go.

00:03:56.950 --> 00:03:59.570
You gonna catch that Pokémon?

00:03:59.570 --> 00:04:02.720
Yeah! The way it hides itself
reminds me of Mew.

00:04:02.720 --> 00:04:04.540
I just gotta catch it, yeah?

00:04:04.540 --> 00:04:06.740
What seems to be the matter?

00:04:06.740 --> 00:04:08.420
Miss Joy!

00:04:08.420 --> 00:04:09.990
And...

00:04:12.340 --> 00:04:17.060
Yessan! Emotion Pokémon!
Psychic/Normal type!

00:04:17.060 --> 00:04:21.550
These intelligent Pokémon use the horns
on their heads to sense the emotions of others!

00:04:21.550 --> 00:04:25.900
Males will act as valets for those they serve,
and the females are particularly good at babysitting!

00:04:26.790 --> 00:04:29.080
Are you searching for something here?

00:04:29.080 --> 00:04:32.750
There was a Pokémon
we’d never seen before, but it ran away.

00:04:32.750 --> 00:04:35.250
It looks like it can
become invisible.

00:04:35.250 --> 00:04:36.960
Invisible?

00:04:36.960 --> 00:04:39.050
It was about this big...

00:04:39.050 --> 00:04:41.960
And it had a crest like this,
and a twirly tail.

00:04:41.960 --> 00:04:44.720
Oh, that must have been Messon.

00:04:44.720 --> 00:04:45.930
Messon?

00:04:45.930 --> 00:04:50.550
Yes. Many can be found living
in areas with lush nature.

00:04:50.550 --> 00:04:56.060
They’re incredibly timid,
so you hardly ever spot Messon in cities.

00:04:56.060 --> 00:04:58.530
I wonder if it got lost.

00:04:58.530 --> 00:04:59.690
Lost?

00:04:59.690 --> 00:05:03.820
If it’s timid...
Does that mean it got afraid and hid?

00:05:03.820 --> 00:05:08.830
Perhaps. Messon becomes invisible
when it touches water,

00:05:08.830 --> 00:05:11.580
so it might be hiding over there.

00:05:13.540 --> 00:05:14.870
A fountain?

00:05:17.580 --> 00:05:20.590
Messon, are you there?

00:05:20.590 --> 00:05:24.850
I’m Go. I really like your ability!

00:05:24.850 --> 00:05:27.340
Wanna come with me?

00:05:28.870 --> 00:05:32.100
We’re not angry
that you ate our breakfast.

00:05:32.650 --> 00:05:35.600
Heck, if you join us,
we can eat together!

00:05:39.020 --> 00:05:40.610
Not there, huh...?

00:05:40.610 --> 00:05:44.020
It might have run
somewhere far away.

00:05:46.160 --> 00:05:48.630
And here I wanted to catch it!

00:05:53.690 --> 00:05:54.770
Oh, no...

00:05:54.770 --> 00:05:58.550
I just tossed a valuable
Monster Ball without thinking!

00:05:58.550 --> 00:06:02.200
Messon’s data will be
added to the Index!

00:06:02.960 --> 00:06:04.260
What?!

00:06:04.260 --> 00:06:06.860
No way! It was right there?!

00:06:09.430 --> 00:06:12.110
Hey... Where are we?

00:06:12.110 --> 00:06:13.840
Not a clue.

00:06:13.840 --> 00:06:17.730
Probably somewhere in Galar,
if my calculations are correct, meow.

00:06:19.650 --> 00:06:23.730
And we had such a great plan
to catch Pikachu, too...

00:06:26.680 --> 00:06:28.400
Then we got blown away,

00:06:28.400 --> 00:06:29.510
and after this...

00:06:30.080 --> 00:06:31.490
...and that...

00:06:31.490 --> 00:06:35.140
...and all kinds of stuff,
we end up in <i>Galar?!</i>

00:06:35.140 --> 00:06:38.760
There’s no way Pikachu
would be here!

00:06:40.000 --> 00:06:42.350
What? Show me, meow!

00:06:42.350 --> 00:06:43.380
What’s up?

00:06:43.380 --> 00:06:47.380
There’s Pikachu, meow!
The brat boys are there, too, meow!

00:06:47.380 --> 00:06:48.210
Seriously?!

00:06:48.210 --> 00:06:49.330
Seriously, meow.

00:06:49.330 --> 00:06:51.520
Our ship has come in!

00:06:52.260 --> 00:06:56.040
Messon! Water Lizard Pokémon!
Water type!

00:06:56.040 --> 00:07:00.180
When it touches water, its body color changes
to blend into its surroundings!

00:07:00.180 --> 00:07:07.920
Because of its timid personality, it can sometimes
turn invisible from its <i>own</i> fluids, such as tears or sweat!

00:07:07.920 --> 00:07:11.070
So that’s why it disappeared
when it cried.

00:07:11.070 --> 00:07:13.630
Aren’t you glad
you managed to catch Messon, Go?

00:07:13.630 --> 00:07:14.810
Yeah.

00:07:21.490 --> 00:07:23.150
Hey, Riolu, what’s wrong?

00:07:23.150 --> 00:07:24.540
What’s that?!

00:07:25.760 --> 00:07:29.500
Sunahebi! Sand Snake Pokémon!
Ground type!

00:07:29.500 --> 00:07:34.930
As it digs, it swallows sand and stores it
in its neck pouch, to spray out later!

00:07:35.310 --> 00:07:37.710
All right!
I’ll catch this one, too!

00:07:37.710 --> 00:07:40.480
Monster Ball, go!

00:07:42.850 --> 00:07:46.550
Didn’t work.
I’ll battle it, then!

00:07:46.550 --> 00:07:49.840
The Water-type Messon
would be a perfect match, yeah?

00:07:49.840 --> 00:07:52.820
That’s right!
I wanna see Messon battle!

00:07:52.820 --> 00:07:53.910
Go, Messon!

00:07:56.600 --> 00:07:57.700
There it is!

00:07:59.480 --> 00:08:02.110
Rotom, what moves
does Messon know?

00:08:02.110 --> 00:08:03.630
These!

00:08:11.930 --> 00:08:12.840
It vanished!

00:08:12.840 --> 00:08:15.200
Sunahebi looks confused!

00:08:15.950 --> 00:08:17.470
Messon! Water Gun!

00:08:27.060 --> 00:08:30.080
Messon!
Once it comes out, use Pound!

00:08:31.870 --> 00:08:33.360
Keep it up, Messon!

00:08:43.480 --> 00:08:45.500
You’re totally visible
because of the sand!

00:08:45.500 --> 00:08:47.990
Messon! Disappear again!

00:08:51.270 --> 00:08:52.590
What’s wrong, Messon?

00:08:52.590 --> 00:08:54.290
It looks troubled.

00:08:54.290 --> 00:08:57.270
Maybe it can’t
disappear at will?

00:09:08.700 --> 00:09:10.190
Again!

00:09:10.190 --> 00:09:13.440
What <i>is</i> this?!

00:09:14.370 --> 00:09:20.080
It’s said that Messon’s tears
pack the chemical punch of 100 onions!

00:09:21.170 --> 00:09:22.830
I see!

00:09:29.080 --> 00:09:32.210
Wait, Messon! Return!

00:09:35.640 --> 00:09:37.950
It ran away... didn’t it?

00:09:38.710 --> 00:09:41.060
We gotta get it back!

00:09:41.060 --> 00:09:42.720
Yeah!

00:09:47.920 --> 00:09:49.390
Where’d it go?

00:09:49.390 --> 00:09:51.060
Well, it can turn invisible...

00:09:54.720 --> 00:09:56.360
There’s loads of people crying!

00:09:56.360 --> 00:09:57.610
It’s that way!

00:10:03.200 --> 00:10:05.080
We’ll look over here.

00:10:05.080 --> 00:10:07.250
We go this way, Rabbifoot!

00:10:09.380 --> 00:10:11.660
Huh? Where’d it go?

00:10:16.630 --> 00:10:17.970
Think this looks suspicious?

00:10:23.650 --> 00:10:26.240
Oh, that’s not it!

00:10:31.340 --> 00:10:33.650
So this is where you were.

00:10:34.590 --> 00:10:37.960
I’m sorry I scared you, Messon.

00:10:44.830 --> 00:10:48.910
Wait, don’t cry!
We won’t do anything to you!

00:10:48.910 --> 00:10:51.460
Okay, Messon?

00:10:59.260 --> 00:11:05.010
We really have to do something about
that “chemical punch of 100 onions” thing.

00:11:08.030 --> 00:11:11.020
Oh, of course!

00:11:13.140 --> 00:11:14.780
Go! Find it?

00:11:15.520 --> 00:11:18.680
I did! But it fled into the river.

00:11:18.680 --> 00:11:20.530
It probably swam downstream!

00:11:20.530 --> 00:11:23.360
Okay! Let’s search along the river!

00:11:25.910 --> 00:11:27.970
Where are we?

00:11:27.970 --> 00:11:30.170
We lost sight of Pikachu...

00:11:30.170 --> 00:11:33.040
He’s definitely <i>somewhere</i>
in the city, meow.

00:11:34.220 --> 00:11:38.430
How do you expect us
to find him in that huge city?!

00:11:43.420 --> 00:11:44.300
What’s that?

00:11:48.780 --> 00:11:49.920
A Pokémon.

00:11:49.920 --> 00:11:52.550
Yeah. One I’ve never seen before.

00:11:52.550 --> 00:11:54.790
Who’s that, meow?

00:11:54.790 --> 00:11:56.120
Morpeko...

00:11:56.120 --> 00:11:57.570
Morpeko?

00:11:57.570 --> 00:11:59.710
What kind of Pokémon is that?

00:11:59.710 --> 00:12:02.880
I just... don’t feel like
explaining it today.

00:12:02.880 --> 00:12:03.390
Cut the attitude and
just do your job!

00:12:03.390 --> 00:12:05.900
Stop! You’ll break it!
Cut the attitude and
just do your job!

00:12:05.900 --> 00:12:06.130
Cut the attitude and
just do your job!

00:12:09.920 --> 00:12:12.330
Our rations!

00:12:12.330 --> 00:12:14.420
What’re you doing
stuffing your face?!

00:12:19.170 --> 00:12:20.680
It got away!

00:12:21.930 --> 00:12:25.220
A dine-and-dash?
Are you kidding me?

00:12:28.100 --> 00:12:30.520
What’s that?

00:12:30.520 --> 00:12:33.060
Messon. That’s a Messon.

00:12:33.060 --> 00:12:34.340
Messon!

00:12:34.340 --> 00:12:35.720
Where are you?

00:12:37.080 --> 00:12:38.340
That voice!

00:12:38.340 --> 00:12:39.500
There’s no doubting it, meow!

00:12:39.500 --> 00:12:40.940
It’s the brat boys and...

00:12:40.940 --> 00:12:42.110
...Pikachu!

00:12:43.480 --> 00:12:46.240
They said “Messon! Where are you?”,
didn’t they?

00:12:46.240 --> 00:12:47.990
That’s right.

00:12:47.990 --> 00:12:50.080
They’re looking for
this thing, meow!

00:12:55.440 --> 00:12:57.340
Pocket Monsters!

00:13:01.590 --> 00:13:06.510
Water
Messon

00:13:06.510 --> 00:13:09.450
Messon! Are you there?

00:13:09.450 --> 00:13:12.120
Please come out, Messon!

00:13:14.390 --> 00:13:17.990
That’s weird...
Did it go even farther?

00:13:17.990 --> 00:13:19.370
It’s my fault.

00:13:21.870 --> 00:13:25.960
I just forced Messon to battle
without considering how it felt.

00:13:26.530 --> 00:13:30.160
Of course it’d run away
from a trainer like me.

00:13:30.160 --> 00:13:31.370
Go.

00:13:32.380 --> 00:13:34.910
Just try harder next time then,
once we find it!

00:13:35.960 --> 00:13:38.140
You only just caught it, right?

00:13:38.140 --> 00:13:40.530
You can’t expect everything
to work out right away.

00:13:41.430 --> 00:13:42.680
Satoshi...

00:13:45.520 --> 00:13:47.180
I guess you’re right!

00:13:47.180 --> 00:13:49.680
Messon, where are you?

00:13:49.680 --> 00:13:50.800
Right here!

00:13:50.800 --> 00:13:51.980
What?

00:13:51.980 --> 00:13:52.560
Where?

00:13:54.060 --> 00:13:57.660
If you ask us
“What? Where?”

00:13:57.660 --> 00:14:00.900
We’ll answer out of
sympathy for the world!

00:14:01.610 --> 00:14:04.000
To protect the world from devastation.

00:14:04.000 --> 00:14:06.580
To preserve world peace.

00:14:07.540 --> 00:14:10.120
Championing the evils
of truth and love.

00:14:10.120 --> 00:14:13.080
We’re the lovely, charming villains.

00:14:13.730 --> 00:14:14.490
Musashi!

00:14:14.490 --> 00:14:15.540
Kojiro!

00:14:16.200 --> 00:14:19.370
The Team Rocket duo
soars through the galaxy!

00:14:19.370 --> 00:14:22.890
Like a white hole,
a white tomorrow awaits us!

00:14:22.890 --> 00:14:25.000
Just kidding, meow!

00:14:28.880 --> 00:14:30.220
Team Rocket!

00:14:30.670 --> 00:14:34.600
Could this perhaps be
what you're looking for?

00:14:36.680 --> 00:14:37.460
Messon!

00:14:37.460 --> 00:14:39.020
How’d you end up
with Team Rocket?!

00:14:39.380 --> 00:14:42.000
We don’t mind
giving it back to you...

00:14:42.000 --> 00:14:45.780
<i>If</i> you give us Pikachu
in exchange!

00:14:55.050 --> 00:14:57.820
Huh...? Weren’t we laughing...?

00:14:57.820 --> 00:14:59.880
So why are we crying...?!

00:14:59.880 --> 00:15:02.180
I don’t know, meow...!

00:15:02.180 --> 00:15:05.310
Anyway, we just want Pikachu!

00:15:06.100 --> 00:15:08.170
Trade us it for Messon!

00:15:08.170 --> 00:15:11.120
Are you kidding?!
You’re not getting Pikachu!

00:15:11.120 --> 00:15:13.090
But we’re taking Messon back!

00:15:14.910 --> 00:15:17.920
Awful! You’re just awful!

00:15:17.920 --> 00:15:20.700
We can’t have either?!
How could you <i>be<u> so cruel?!</u></i>

00:15:20.700 --> 00:15:24.260
Poor us, meow!

00:15:27.360 --> 00:15:28.910
It kinda feels like...

00:15:28.910 --> 00:15:31.000
...<i>we’re</i> the bad guys...

00:15:33.790 --> 00:15:36.840
Aaah, just stop crying already!

00:15:36.840 --> 00:15:40.860
Your crying makes <i>us</i> cry, too!

00:15:42.610 --> 00:15:44.310
If you won’t hand him over...

00:15:44.310 --> 00:15:46.000
Then we’ll just take him by force!

00:15:46.430 --> 00:15:48.580
Vending, come on!

00:15:57.070 --> 00:15:58.780
Rocket...

00:15:58.780 --> 00:16:00.400
Vending...

00:16:01.440 --> 00:16:03.190
Secret!

00:16:03.190 --> 00:16:04.580
Time to battle!

00:16:04.580 --> 00:16:06.110
Go!

00:16:09.490 --> 00:16:11.570
The Magnetic Field Pokémon,
Jibacoil!

00:16:13.570 --> 00:16:16.070
The Plate Pokémon,
Armaldo!

00:16:18.990 --> 00:16:20.910
We’re gonna save Messon!

00:16:20.910 --> 00:16:22.880
Rabbifoot! Double Kick!

00:16:23.860 --> 00:16:27.670
Pikachu! Lightning Speed!
Riolu, you use Shadow Clones!

00:16:30.670 --> 00:16:32.900
Armaldo! Metal Claw!

00:16:32.900 --> 00:16:34.390
Jibacoil! Supersonic Waves!

00:16:52.830 --> 00:16:57.380
See? This is what you get
for not handing over Pikachu!

00:16:57.380 --> 00:17:01.990
Why would you try so hard to get
this weak crybaby Pokémon back, anyway?

00:17:01.990 --> 00:17:04.450
Are you complete morons?

00:17:04.450 --> 00:17:08.750
Be quiet! Messon might be
a crybaby, but it is <i>not</i> “weak”!

00:17:10.880 --> 00:17:14.850
Hang on, Messon!
I promise I’ll save you!

00:17:17.800 --> 00:17:19.080
You feisty little brat!

00:17:19.080 --> 00:17:22.160
Jibacoil, keep firing your
Supersonic Waves!

00:17:26.500 --> 00:17:30.270
Messon...
I’ll save you right now!

00:17:45.270 --> 00:17:48.170
Messon, are you there?

00:17:48.170 --> 00:17:52.190
I’m Go. I really like your ability!

00:17:52.190 --> 00:17:54.930
Wanna come with me?

00:18:11.370 --> 00:18:12.410
What?

00:18:13.180 --> 00:18:15.490
It got out, meow!

00:18:17.370 --> 00:18:19.740
That’s why I said
not to use a cheap cage!

00:18:19.740 --> 00:18:22.870
We couldn’t <i>afford</i>
a better one on our budget!

00:18:28.870 --> 00:18:30.130
There!

00:18:30.130 --> 00:18:32.360
Messon, over here! Run!

00:18:33.180 --> 00:18:34.040
Kojiro, it’s getting away!

00:18:34.040 --> 00:18:35.090
Hold it!

00:18:35.090 --> 00:18:35.960
Messon!

00:18:39.590 --> 00:18:41.220
Good job, Armaldo!

00:18:45.970 --> 00:18:47.550
Again!

00:18:47.550 --> 00:18:49.350
Satoshi, take these!

00:18:56.720 --> 00:18:59.860
Look at that!
Jibacoil isn’t crying at all!

00:19:01.230 --> 00:19:03.120
Neither is Armaldo!

00:19:05.230 --> 00:19:07.750
...Or so we thought,
but it’s crying its eyes out!

00:19:09.290 --> 00:19:11.000
<i>Those</i> are its eyes?!

00:19:13.870 --> 00:19:18.010
But that must mean
the brat boys have it just as bad!

00:19:20.950 --> 00:19:22.930
I see... Goggles, huh?

00:19:22.930 --> 00:19:23.510
Yeah!

00:19:23.950 --> 00:19:26.390
Since it said
“the chemical punch of 100 onions”,

00:19:26.870 --> 00:19:29.390
I thought back to
Barrierd cooking!

00:19:32.710 --> 00:19:34.640
Guess we owe
Barrierd our thanks!

00:19:34.640 --> 00:19:35.730
That’s right!

00:19:35.730 --> 00:19:37.150
No way!

00:19:37.150 --> 00:19:38.710
Go, now’s our chance!

00:19:38.710 --> 00:19:40.190
Yeah! Let’s fight back!

00:19:40.190 --> 00:19:41.510
Riolu! Vacuum Wave!

00:19:41.510 --> 00:19:42.810
Rabbifoot! Ember!

00:19:42.810 --> 00:19:44.370
Pikachu! 100,000 Volts!

00:19:53.690 --> 00:19:55.750
<i>What an awful feeling!</i>

00:20:02.930 --> 00:20:03.920
Messon.

00:20:05.830 --> 00:20:09.040
I’m sorry I tried to
make you battle.

00:20:10.790 --> 00:20:15.650
Next time I’ll make sure to ask
if you <i>want</i> to battle or not first.

00:20:17.310 --> 00:20:21.330
Your timidness
taught me something.

00:20:23.890 --> 00:20:27.480
You’re always alert, right?

00:20:27.480 --> 00:20:32.070
That way you can always protect yourself
or your friends if need be!

00:20:32.980 --> 00:20:35.920
And so you may be timid,
but you’re not weak!

00:20:36.340 --> 00:20:38.060
You are strong!

00:20:40.170 --> 00:20:43.230
No! Don’t cry!

00:20:44.890 --> 00:20:49.630
Go has caught Messon,
and strengthened their bond just a tiny bit.

00:20:49.630 --> 00:20:53.290
Satoshi and Go’s adventures
will continue!

00:20:55.510 --> 00:20:58.540
This is the absolute pits.

00:20:58.540 --> 00:21:01.890
We couldn’t catch Pikachu, either.

00:21:01.890 --> 00:21:04.240
What a huge waste of time, meow.

00:21:07.510 --> 00:21:08.980
Huh? Pikachu?!

00:21:08.980 --> 00:21:09.700
What?!

00:21:11.450 --> 00:21:14.520
Oh, just that thing again?

00:21:19.210 --> 00:21:21.840
It’s saying “Gimme food!”, meow.

00:21:21.840 --> 00:21:25.340
We’re <i>out</i> of food!
You ate everything we had.

00:21:25.340 --> 00:21:26.760
Scram!

00:21:29.220 --> 00:21:31.720
Oh, dear...
I’ve got kind of an...

00:21:31.720 --> 00:21:33.600
...awful feeling...

00:21:40.160 --> 00:21:42.540
<i>No way!</i>

